-- title:
--   The identity endomorphism X is an automorphism of a formal group law
-- statement:
--   Let $R$ be a commutative ring, $I\subseteq R$ an ideal such that $R$ is $I$-adically complete, and let $F$ be a one-parameter formal group law over $R$, given by its two-variable power series $F.\mathrm{toPowerSeries}$ with vanishing constant coefficient. The assertion is that there exists an isomorphism $\psi$ of $F$ with itself in the sense of the project's `LawIso`: a one-variable power series $\psi.\mathrm{series}$ over $R$ with constant coefficient $0$, whose linear coefficient $\mathrm{coeff}_1$ is a unit of $R$, and which satisfies the homomorphism identity that substituting $F.\mathrm{toPowerSeries}$ into $\psi.\mathrm{series}$ agrees with substituting the pair $(\mathrm{substX}\,0\,\psi.\mathrm{series},\ \mathrm{substX}\,1\,\psi.\mathrm{series})$ into $F.\mathrm{toPowerSeries}$; and this $\psi$ may be taken with two further properties: its series is literally the variable, $\psi.\mathrm{series} =$ `PowerSeries.X`, and the induced map on points is the identity on $I$, i.e. for every $y \in I$ the $I$-adic evaluation `ψ.toLawHom.appAdic I y`, obtained by evaluating $\psi.\mathrm{series}$ at $y$ in the $I$-adically complete ring $R$, equals $y$.
--
--   This records that the identity power series defines an automorphism of any formal group law and that the associated transport of points fixes every element of the defining ideal. It is a piece of formal-group plumbing used in the study of universal deformation rings with Drinfeld level structure, in particular in the identification of the maximal ideal of such a ring with the ideal generated by the two basis parameters.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_FormalGroup_exists_lawIso_refl_appAdic_eq_of_mem.lean

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_FormalGroup_NSeries
import Definitions.Def_FormalGroup_DrinfeldBasis
import Definitions.Def_FormalGroup_PointTransport

set_option maxHeartbeats 4000000
set_option synthInstance.maxHeartbeats 400000
set_option backward.isDefEq.respectTransparency.types false

set_option autoImplicit false

open FormalGroup IsLocalRing

theorem FormalGroup.exists_lawIso_refl_appAdic_eq_of_mem
    {R : Type*} [CommRing R] (I : Ideal R) [IsAdicComplete I R] (F : FormalGroup R) :
    ∃ ψ : FormalGroup.LawIso F F, ψ.series = PowerSeries.X ∧ ∀ y ∈ I, ψ.toLawHom.appAdic I y = y := by sorry
